@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+---
+title: 0.2.0
+description: Publish generic source records and footprints without declared 3D models.
+sidebar_position: 2
+pagination_next: null
+---
+
+Released: 2026-10-02
+
+## Breaking Changes
+
+- Package references and component descriptors now represent an absent 3D model
+  with explicit null model-path, transform and descriptor fields. TypeScript
+  consumers must check for null before reading model paths or transforms.
+- Document-kind consumers must handle the new `source-record` variant.
+
+## Features
+
+- Select a reviewed non-PDF source under the label **Source record**, preserving
+  its title, authority and availability without calling it a datasheet.
+- Publish a mapped footprint when it contains no model declaration. The page
+  retains its footprint preview and states that 3D geometry and physical fit
+  remain unverified; it creates no model viewer, download or request.
+
+## Bug Fixes
+
+- Keep declared missing, malformed, duplicate or unsafe model references fatal,
+  including declarations with whitespace before the model token. Accept legacy
+  KiCad module roots and read transforms only from the actual model declaration.
+- Include footprint-only pages in browser checks, retain a model-bearing
+  representative when available, and report skipped model interactions honestly.
+
+Existing source, footprint, pin-map and declared-model checks remain in force.
+These publication options do not establish component applicability or physical
+qualification.
